<SiteLayout title="Real 5GC Interfaces and Evidence" lang="en" description="Real 5GC request/response contracts, correlation keys, fact authority and acceptance evidence.">
<section class="hero"><span class="eyebrow">Interfaces / Evidence</span><h1>Real 5GC interfaces and evidence</h1><p class="lede">For each interface, this guide explains what it can prove, how requests and state are correlated, and what is required before PASS is justified. Owner schemas and code define fields; unfrozen interfaces are marked rather than guessed.</p><p><a href="/en/runbooks/real-5gc/">Real 5GC runbook →</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>1. Four kinds of facts must remain distinct</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Authority</th><th>Can prove</th><th>Cannot prove alone</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>5GC business state</td><td>Open5GS inspection, normalized by Provider</td><td>UE registration and source-defined session fields.</td><td>HTTP 200 or <code>pdu_state=active</code> does not prove session established, QoS satisfaction or user-plane reachability.</td></tr><tr><td>Protocol/network observation</td><td><code>env-fabric</code></td><td>Boundary requests/responses, protocol transactions, endpoints, direction and fault receipts.</td><td>Cannot replace current Open5GS state or prove remote commit because a request was observed.</td></tr><tr><td>Execution facts and Predicate</td><td><code>ca-runtime</code></td><td>Run/Invocation, admitted binding, evidence and PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN.</td><td>A 2xx response cannot skip postconditions, reconciliation or user-plane checks.</td></tr><tr><td>Final experiment verdict</td><td>Sandbox / Benchmark evaluator</td><td>Replayable verdict from a frozen scenario and independent evidence.</td><td>Agent self-report or a test fixture is not independent Ground Truth.</td></tr>
</tbody></table><p>Sandbox composes environments and acceptance; each owner retains fact authority. Runtime binds directly to the actual fact owner rather than relaying every fact through Sandbox. An independent Oracle adjudicates the final experiment.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>2. Interface inventory and maturity</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Method / contract</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>AMF inspection</td><td><code>GET http://10.30.20.5:9090/ue-info?page=N&amp;page_size=100</code></td><td>Existing Open5GS v2.8.0 read-only surface; pagination and HTTP 200 do not imply an atomic snapshot.</td></tr><tr><td>SMF inspection</td><td><code>GET http://10.30.20.4:9090/pdu-info</code></td><td><code>pdu_state=active</code> is not canonical session-established.</td></tr><tr><td>Provider Observation</td><td><code>POST /v1/observations/read</code>; <code>connectionagent.provider-observation/v1</code></td><td>Accepted scope is UE registration v0.1 only, not session/QoS/connectivity.</td></tr><tr><td>Fabric Network Observation</td><td><code>POST /v1/observations/query</code>; <code>service-fabric.v1alpha1</code></td><td>Queries network/protocol events; PARTIAL_GAP is not complete evidence.</td></tr><tr><td>Fetch one Fabric event</td><td><code>GET /v1/events/{fabricEventRef}</code></td><td>Use only event refs returned by a query.</td></tr><tr><td>R2-B consume/execute</td><td>Owner lane; execution identity <code>actionRef + expectedRevision</code></td><td>Governed path, not R1 observation API. No unfrozen body or generic stable route is invented here.</td></tr>
</tbody></table><p>See the <a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-provider-5gc/blob/main/docs/design/real-open5gs-provider-contract.md">Provider / Fact Contract</a> and <a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/env-fabric/blob/main/schemas/v1alpha1/service-fabric.openapi.yaml">Fabric OpenAPI</a>.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>3. Open5GS read-only state</h2><h3>AMF registration facts</h3><p>Owner: Open5GS AMF; endpoint <code>http://10.30.20.5:9090/ue-info</code>. The Provider reads bounded pages and matches an explicit SUPI. Raw SUPI and response bodies must not appear in public logs or sanitized manifests.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Source condition</th><th>Accepted meaning</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mm_state=registered</code></td><td><code>registrationState=REGISTERED</code></td><td>Based on pinned source enum and accepted registration contract.</td></tr><tr><td>Explicit source-defined deregistered state</td><td><code>DEREGISTERED</code></td><td>Unknown/transient MM states must not map to deregistered.</td></tr><tr><td>No match, page gap, duplicate identity, invalid response or timeout</td><td>Apply Provider resolution; insufficient evidence becomes Runtime UNKNOWN.</td><td>An empty page cannot automatically become KNOWN_NEGATIVE.</td></tr><tr><td><code>snapshotConsistency=NOT_PROVIDED</code></td><td>Source provides no snapshot-consistency guarantee.</td><td>Multi-page results are not an atomic snapshot.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>SMF session context</h3><p>Owner: Open5GS SMF; endpoint <code>http://10.30.20.4:9090/pdu-info</code>. Observable fields include SUPI, PDU Session ID, DNN, S-NSSAI, addresses, QoS flows and N3 summaries; pinned source defines actual output.</p><p><strong>Forbidden inference:</strong> <code>pdu_state=active</code> is not session-established; QoS-flow presence does not prove QoS satisfaction; an address/TEID does not prove user-plane reachability. Current inspection does not provide snapshot consistency or PFCP subject correlation.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>4. Provider Observation v1</h2><p>The registration service endpoint is deployment-configured. The example listens on <code>10.30.20.1:8080</code> and reads <code>http://10.30.20.5:9090/ue-info</code>. Bind address must be an explicit non-wildcard IP; egress URL must exactly match its allowlist.</p><h3>Request: <code>POST /v1/observations/read</code></h3><pre><code>{
  "apiVersion": "connectionagent.io/v1alpha1",
  "kind": "ProviderObservationReadRequest",
  "contractVersion": "connectionagent.provider-observation/v1",
  "spec": {
    "observationRef": "ue.registration.snapshot",
    "identities": { "5gc.supi": "001010000000001" },
    "runtimeRunId": "run-reference",
    "invocationId": "invocation-reference"
  }
}</code></pre><p>The SUPI is a format example, not a real UE identity. Canonical SUPI is 15 digits; missing/invalid identity must not trigger an upstream read.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>apiVersion/kind/contractVersion</code></td><td>Strict contract identity; unknown fields and duplicate JSON keys should be rejected.</td></tr><tr><td><code>observationRef</code></td><td>Fixed to <code>ue.registration.snapshot</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>identities["5gc.supi"]</code></td><td>Explicit subject; episodeRef, nickname or fuzzy identity is not a substitute.</td></tr><tr><td><code>runtimeRunId/invocationId</code></td><td>Correlates Runtime Run and read invocation; response echoes both unchanged.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Response: <code>ProviderObservationReadResult</code></h3><pre><code>{
  "apiVersion": "connectionagent.io/v1alpha1",
  "kind": "ProviderObservationReadResult",
  "contractVersion": "connectionagent.provider-observation/v1",
  "spec": {
    "observationRef": "ue.registration.snapshot",
    "sourceRef": "env-5gc-real",
    "runtimeRunId": "run-reference",
    "invocationId": "invocation-reference",
    "resolution": "FOUND",
    "observation": {
      "status": "OBSERVED",
      "present": true,
      "valid": true,
      "value": { "registrationState": "REGISTERED" },
      "evidence": ["open5gs-amf-page-count=1", "open5gs-amf-item-count=1", "open5gs-amf-snapshot-consistency=NOT_PROVIDED"],
      "observedAt": "2026-10-21T05:28:27.348538481Z"
    }
  }
}</code></pre><p>Field-shape example only. sourceRef, Run/Invocation IDs, resolution and evidence must come from the actual result, never hardcoded to PASS.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Resolution</th><th>Handling</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>FOUND</code></td><td>Fact found and normalized; Runtime still validates source, binding and freshness before Predicate evaluation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>KNOWN_NEGATIVE</code></td><td>Only when permitted by contract and backed by an authoritative negative fact; an empty page is insufficient.</td></tr><tr><td><code>UNAVAILABLE</code></td><td>Source unavailable, incomplete read or indeterminate state; typically Predicate UNKNOWN.</td></tr><tr><td><code>INVALID_QUERY</code></td><td>Invalid identity/query input, not a negative business-state result.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The accepted wire fact is UE registration only. Do not describe it as a delivered session/QoS/connectivity API.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>5. Fabric Network Observation</h2><p>Business routes are defined by the owner <a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/env-fabric/blob/main/schemas/v1alpha1/service-fabric.openapi.yaml">OpenAPI</a>; the management listener uses separate <code>/management/v1/*</code> routes.</p><h3>Query: <code>POST /v1/observations/query</code></h3><pre><code>{
  "apiVersion": "connectionagent.io/v1alpha1",
  "kind": "NetworkObservationQuery",
  "contractVersion": "service-fabric.v1alpha1",
  "spec": {
    "filter": {
      "acquisitionMode": "REAL_INLINE",
      "interface": "N4",
      "protocol": "PFCP",
      "messageKind": "PFCP_SESSION_ESTABLISHMENT_REQUEST",
      "direction": "REQUEST"
    },
    "pageSize": 100
  }
}</code></pre><p>This is a PFCP query example. Real acceptance must add required environment/generation/transaction filters from the active profile; it is not the default R1 SBI query.</p><p><code>NetworkObservationResult</code> includes <code>queryRef</code>, <code>availability</code> (<code>COMPLETE</code>/<code>PARTIAL_GAP</code>/<code>UNAVAILABLE</code>), owner-native <code>records[]</code> (<code>FabricEvent</code>), optional <code>nextCursor</code>, <code>gapReasonCode</code> and <code>sourceAuthority=env-fabric</code>.</p><table><thead><tr><th>FabricEvent field</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>fabricEventRef/messageRef</code></td><td>Owner event/message identity.</td><td>Preserve values; fetch with <code>GET /v1/events/{fabricEventRef}</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>transactionRef</code></td><td>Fabric transaction correlation.</td><td>Do not merge request/response from different transactions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>protocol/messageKind/direction</code></td><td>Protocol, message kind and direction.</td><td>Must match scenario; request is not response.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sourceEndpointRef/destinationEndpointRef</code></td><td>Endpoint relationship.</td><td>Validate against owner endpoint identity.</td></tr><tr><td><code>subjectRefs/correlationRefs</code></td><td>Explicit subject/cross-record link.</td><td>Do not fill missing links by guessing or timestamp proximity.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ownerSequence</code></td><td>Monotonic owner-domain sequence.</td><td>Do not conflate with SRF seqNo, Runtime invocation ID or NAS sequence.</td></tr><tr><td><code>recordDigest/payloadAvailability</code></td><td>Record integrity and payload availability.</td><td>Digest does not prove business action success.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Associating PFCP with a UE/PDU Session requires accepted SUPI+PSI to SMF/UPF F-SEID correlation. Timestamp proximity, endpoint match or event existence alone is insufficient.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>6. R2-B NetworkIntent and exact action</h2><p>R1 does not publish NetworkIntent, hold requests or call Agent/Harness. R2-B must use the <a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/connectionagent/blob/main/contracts/schemas/network-intent-v2.schema.yaml">canonical NetworkIntent v2</a>; do not copy fields from older v1 design text.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Acceptance rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>intentRef</code></td><td>Semantic event identity.</td><td>Non-empty and unique in source context.</td></tr><tr><td><code>actionRef + revision</code></td><td>Fabric held action and version.</td><td>State HELD; exact revision match; no re-resolution or substitute action.</td></tr><tr><td><code>episodeRef</code></td><td>Workflow correlation.</td><td>Correlation only, not Open5GS state authority.</td></tr><tr><td><code>source.origin/source.boundary</code></td><td>Protocol provenance; first lane is AMF/SBI.</td><td><code>sourceName=SRF</code> does not replace provenance.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sourceName/timestampUs/seqNo</code></td><td>SRF label, first-ingress time and SRF sequence.</td><td>Preserve separately; timestamp is Unix epoch microseconds; seqNo is not NAS security sequence.</td></tr><tr><td><code>subjectRef/request.pduSessionId</code></td><td>Logical subject and PDU Session ID.</td><td>Must match the same UE/session; unaccepted source locator is not canonical subject.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sourceRefs</code></td><td>References to source material retained by Fabric.</td><td>Do not copy raw SBI/N1 into a second authority.</td></tr><tr><td><code>deadline</code></td><td>Action expiry.</td><td>Check at admission and execution; fail closed when expired.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The first PDU Session lane requires <code>operation=PDU_SESSION/ESTABLISH</code>, <code>source.origin=AMF</code>, <code>source.boundary=SBI</code>, <code>messageType=193 (0xC1)</code>, <code>requestType=1 (INITIAL_REQUEST)</code>, plus exact held state, revision, deadline and subject/session scope.</p><p>Execution identity is frozen as <code>execute(actionRef, expectedRevision)</code>. Actual JSON body, HTTP route and receipt fields must come from the current Fabric R2-B owner schema/host profile. If absent, do not invent them or substitute R1's observations query route.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>7. Runtime: Observation to Predicate</h2><pre><code>Skill PredicateDefinition
  -> Runtime resolves admitted binding
  -> ObservationSource acquires from fact owner
  -> normalized observation + provenance/evidence
  -> Runtime validates source/binding/freshness
  -> Predicate evaluator
  -> PASS / FAIL / UNKNOWN
  -> Runtime Outcome / Reconcile where applicable</code></pre><table><thead><tr><th>Field/input</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>sourceRef</code> and binding identity/digest</td><td>ObservationSource + Runtime binding resolution</td><td>Must match deployment expectation; missing/mismatched provenance fails closed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>observationRef</code>, normalized value</td><td>Provider normalizes; Runtime validates contract.</td><td>Unknown source enums must not be guessed into PASS/FAIL values.</td></tr><tr><td><code>observedAt</code> / freshness</td><td>Source timestamp + Runtime freshness policy.</td><td>Stale/missing required time means reacquire or UNKNOWN.</td></tr><tr><td><code>evidence[]</code> / source refs</td><td>Owner supplies evidence; Runtime associates it with Run/Invocation.</td><td>Avoid exposing SUPI, keys, tokens or unnecessary sensitive fields.</td></tr><tr><td>Provider knowledge / transport error</td><td>Provider returns knowledge/unavailability; Runtime determines Outcome.</td><td>After possible mutation dispatch, do not blindly replay an ambiguous result; preserve <code>OUTCOME_UNKNOWN</code> and reconcile by policy.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Agent-visible read-only ToolResult is planning input, not Predicate PASS. Provider does not produce Predicate verdicts; ObservationSource does not own underlying truth; Agent does not call Provider directly or write authoritative Outcome.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>8. Minimum acceptance evidence</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Minimum evidence</th><th>If missing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>UE registered</td><td>Real UE state, AMF /ue-info semantics, Provider request/result, normalized Observation and Predicate verdict from the same Runtime invocation.</td><td>UNKNOWN; gNB connection or SBI traffic alone is insufficient.</td></tr><tr><td>PDU Session established</td><td>Owner-accepted AMF/SMF state semantics, correlated CreateSMContext request/response, PFCP transaction and same-UE/session keys.</td><td>Do not infer from <code>pdu_state=active</code> alone.</td></tr><tr><td>Governed action executed</td><td>NetworkIntent v2, sourceRefs, actionRef/revision/deadline, admission result, exact execution receipt and correlated response.</td><td>No PASS without exact receipt or unambiguous correlation.</td></tr><tr><td>User plane reachable</td><td>Active session/TUN-up evidence plus source interface, target, command, exit code and packet results.</td><td>UPF gateway ping does not imply external Internet reachability.</td></tr><tr><td>Final experiment passes</td><td>Frozen scenario/run manifest, owner evidence, cleanup CLOSED, independent evaluator verdict and replayable inputs.</td><td>Inconsistent/open-window evidence is unjudgeable/invalid, not automatic PASS/FAIL.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Manifests should record repository/upstream commits and digests, profile/config digest, host/run identity, time window, schema/contract versions, Run/Invocation, sourceRef/binding digest, event/transaction/action refs, result and cleanup status. Keep sensitive raw payloads out of public docs; retain digests, field/type reports and controlled-storage references.</p></section>
